__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
exps
common_utils/build/
.vscode
wandb
data/
# NOT covered by `data/` above: a trailing slash matches DIRECTORIES only, so it
# never matched `release/data` when that path is a SYMLINK -- which is how a link
# pointing into one developer's personal scratch got committed once. Worse, the
# `data/` rule DOES match a real `release/data/` dir, making its contents IGNORED
# rather than untracked, and git silently DELETES ignored files to make room for a
# tracked path. Anyone who pulled lost that directory with no warning. This path is
# per-machine storage config: create it yourself (docs/setup.md 1).
release/data
*.png
*.pdf
*.mp4
*.gif
.env
release/model
*.zip

# ---- 大文件：日志 / 权重 / 数据集（本地保留，不入库）----
*.log
logs/
MUJOCO_LOG.TXT
nohup.out

